import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 292 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Critique of Realm Inflation: Setting Collapse of a Dozen-Plus Realms","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 292 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Critique of Realm Inflation: Setting Collapse of a Dozen-Plus Realms","no":292,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Realm Inflation","Setting Collapse","Law-First Axiom","Plot Kidnaps Setting"],"related":["14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0292_模块2-遮天-境界膨胀批判.md","filePath":"en/0292_模块2-遮天-境界膨胀批判.md"}'),o={name:"en/0292_模块2-遮天-境界膨胀批判.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,d,u){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-292-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-critique-of-realm-inflation-setting-collapse-of-a-dozen-plus-realms" tabindex="-1">Entry 292 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Critique of Realm Inflation: Setting Collapse of a Dozen-Plus Realms <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-292-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-critique-of-realm-inflation-setting-collapse-of-a-dozen-plus-realms" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 292 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Critique of Realm Inflation: Setting Collapse of a Dozen-Plus Realms&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 5) | Benchmark base: Documents 14, 97, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-realms-are-no-longer-a-ladder-just-clay-in-the-author-s-hand" tabindex="-1">Introduction: When realms are no longer a ladder, just clay in the author&#39;s hand <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-realms-are-no-longer-a-ladder-just-clay-in-the-author-s-hand" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: When realms are no longer a ladder, just clay in the author&#39;s hand&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> is core — laws first, never retcon, setting self-consistency over plot convenience. This entry is precisely the law-first axiom&#39;s direct range: Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; realm system (Sea of Wheels → Dao Palace → Four Extremes → Dragon Transformation → Immortal Platform → Saint → Saint King → Great Sage → Quasi-Emperor → Emperor → Red-Dust Immortal, a dozen-plus tiers) is a classic sample of long-web-novel realm inflation. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Realm inflation itself is a narrative energy waste:</p><ul><li>Every new realm added voids readers&#39; early cognition that &quot;this tier is already strong&quot;</li><li>The author must constantly explain &quot;why the new realm is so much stronger than the old,&quot; explanation cost skyrockets</li><li>Readers lose number intuition; &quot;who wins&quot; is no longer calculated by realm, but decided by plot emotion — narrative predictive power zeroes out</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Realm inflation&#39;s regression at the civilization-narrative level:</p><ol><li><strong>Strong-one inflation</strong>: Saint, Saint King, Great Sage batch-appear late; early &quot;saint immortal&quot; scarcity collapses</li><li><strong>Historical sense diluted</strong>: each era&#39;s &quot;emperor&quot; count is unclear; ancient history becomes a fuzzy legend</li><li><strong>Comparability lost</strong>: readers cannot judge a battle&#39;s weight; civilization epic degrades to emotion-flow</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking behind realm inflation:</p><ul><li><strong>Predation on reader expectations</strong>: the author constantly tears up early promises, treating readers&#39; hard-built number intuition as a vault to draw from freely</li><li><strong>Predation on old settings</strong>: early carefully designed Sea of Wheels four layers (Life Spring, Divine Bridge, Dao Platform, Other Shore) late degrade to &quot;newbie village,&quot; design output cheaply consumed</li><li><strong>Predation on supporting-character dignity</strong>: supporting characters once appear are crushed by higher realms; all previous characters&#39; historical achievements devalue</li></ul><p>From another angle, realm inflation is essentially the author using quantity to cover quality. Why were early Sea of Wheels, Dao Palace good? Because every layer had concrete cultivation methods, concrete resource requirements, concrete breakthrough risks; readers could calculate what the protagonist must pay to reach which step. By late, every new realm means only &quot;stronger,&quot; no longer means new cultivation logic — realms change from ladder to scale marks. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s nine-realm cap design philosophy: even if each realm only has five sub-stages, every step must have thresholds, risks, costs. Realm dignity comes from calculability, not from big numbers.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Shrouding&#39;s Dozen-Plus Inflation</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Nine + Two Stable Framework</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Realms keep increasing with plot</td><td>Sense Origin → Condensed Origin → Transform Origin → Law Origin → Dao Origin → Dao Integration → Boundary-Breaking → World-Creation → Origin, nine-realm cap</td></tr><tr><td>Each layer&#39;s strong/weak vague</td><td>Each realm promotion has clear law thresholds and assessments</td></tr><tr><td>New realm overturns old cognition</td><td>New dimensions (Multiverse, Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse) interface as appendix incrementally, not overturning old settings</td></tr><tr><td>Combat power decided by plot</td><td>Combat power law-anchored, calculable</td></tr><tr><td>Setting serves plot</td><td>Laws first, plot must not kidnap setting</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; realm count and each layer&#39;s &quot;combat-weight&quot; curve over chapters</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: compare &quot;constant nine-realm framework&quot; vs. &quot;continuously inflating framework&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: readers&#39; predictive accuracy on numbers, setting-patch count</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: inflating framework late-stage patch count rises exponentially, self-consistency cliff-drops — precisely the ending the law-first axiom must root out</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. Early Sea of Wheels, Dao Palace layering is fine; late Immortal Platform, Saint, Quasi-Emperor, Emperor, Red-Dust Immortal layers padded; realms degrade to emotion tools</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. A dozen-plus realms are themselves a retcon hotbed</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: medium</strong>. Realm inflation mainly serves Ye Fan&#39;s continued-leveling narrative need</li></ul><p>We must also see realm inflation and protagonist-uniqueness dependency mutually reinforce. The more realms inflate, the more the protagonist must constantly break through to maintain &quot;strongest&quot; status; the stronger the protagonist, the more he needs new realms to prove his strength. The two form positive feedback until the whole system blows up. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s nine-realm cap precisely institutionally cuts this positive feedback — no matter how strong the protagonist, he stays within nine realms; reaching the top is the top, no need to add layers for &quot;stronger.&quot;</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: narrative explanation cost and reader predictive power zeroed out</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: predating readers&#39; trust in early settings</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least capped at fierce realm without inflation; Shrouding blows from Sea of Wheels all the way to Red-Dust Immortal, inflation far exceeds Tang Luo</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the more realm tiers, the more closed the top, the less mid-low tiers see a ceiling</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: unstable realm framework cannot support cross-multiverse expansion</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>More realms does not mean a grander world-view. Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; lesson: when layer count grows so many that rules fail, grandeur becomes nothing but vague. Heng Yuan Zhou using a nine-realm cap is not small vision, but daring to let rules call the shots.</p><p>Returning to the law-first axiom&#39;s core: settings are not the author&#39;s private property, but a contract signed with readers. Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; late realm inflation is essentially unilaterally tearing up the contract. Heng Yuan Zhou would rather write fewer layers than let the contract always remain valid.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · realm inflation critique described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./297_模块2-遮天-剧情绑架设定案例.html">Entry 297 · Plot Kidnaps Setting Cases</a> · <a href="./309_模块2-遮天-境界体系替代.html">Entry 309 · Realm System Alternative</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const g=t(o,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
